  <title>5.8.3: Using Function Language and Notation</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01389</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.8.3: Using Function Language and Notation</md:title>
    <md:uuid>6b548f6a-d1b4-43fd-9c14-bf333f06b36b</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>An exponential function is written in the form \(f(x)=ab^x\), where \(a\) is the initial value and \(b\) is the growth factor.</para>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> In a biology lab, a population of 50 bacteria reproduce by splitting. Every hour, on the hour, each bacterium splits into two bacteria.</para>
      
      <para> Write a sentence of the form “_____ is a function of _____.”</para>
      </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> The number of bacteria is a function of time passed in hours. </para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> Indicate which is the independent and which is the dependent variable. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> Independent: number of hours. Dependent: number of bacteria. </para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> Write an equation that represents the situation using function notation. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(
      f(t)=50 \cdot 2^t\) </para>
  </solution></exercise>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Every year after a new car is purchased, it loses \(\frac13\) of its value. Let’s say that the new car costs $18,000.</para>
      
      <para> Write a sentence of the form “_____ is a function of _____.”</para>
      </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> The value of a car is a function of the number of years since purchase. </para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> Indicate which is the independent and which is the dependent variable. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> Independent: number of years since purchase of car. Dependent: value of car in dollars. </para>
  </solution></exercise>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> Write an equation that represents the situation using function notation. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(
      f(t)=18,000 \cdot (\frac{2}{3})^t\). Note: \(\frac13\) is the rate, and growth factor \(=1-\) rate, so the growth factor is \(\frac23\) because there’s \(\frac23\) left. </para>
  </solution></exercise>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>To control an algae bloom in a lake, scientists introduce some treatment products. The day they begin treatment, the area covered by algae is 240 square yards. Each day since the treatment began, a third of the previous day’s area (in square yards) remains covered by algae. Time \(t\) is measured in days.</para>
      
      <para> Write a sentence of the form “_____ is a function of _____.”</para>
      </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> The area covered by algae is a function of the number of days since the treatment. </para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> Indicate which is the independent and which is the dependent variable. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>Independent: number of days since treatment. Dependent: area of algae in square yards.</para>
  </solution></exercise>


<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> Write an equation that represents the situation using function notation. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(
      f(t)=240 \cdot (\frac{1}{3})^t\). Note: \(\frac13\) is given as the growth factor because it represents what remains.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

